;; og:preserve-this function collide-list-fill-bg-using-box is deferred, not
;; landed. Compiles clean through offline-test's narrower context (which does not
;; exercise the full game.gp rlet/macro environment), but (mi) rejects it: past a
;; hand-corrected matrix4h vector4h/long tie (same class as main-collide's
;; instance-sphere-box-intersect?, fixed the same way there), vitof12.xyzw fails
;; with "No method or function named vitof12.xyzw for type object", meaning some
;; vf register in this function's own VU macro block is missing its rlet :class vf
;; declaration in the printed text. The decompiler's own decode does not flag this
;; as a decode error (it is a real compile-time gap, not a decode ambiguity), so
;; the earlier partial hand-fix is not enough on its own; reverted to fully
;; deferred rather than land a function proven not to compile under (mi).
;;   (defun collide-list-fill-bg-using-box ((arg0 collide-cache) (arg1 collide-list) (arg2 collide-query))
;;     ...
;;     )
;; The collide-cache rung activated the extern below (matching the hinted
;; signature already carried in all-types.gc): collide-cache-method-12
;; (fill-using-bounding-box, goal_src/jakx/engine/collide/collide-cache.gc)
;; passes this symbol by name as fill-from-bg's own arg1 callback, the same
;; shape as jak3's own twin. That call site is unreachable today (method 12's
;; own vtable target, collide-cache-method-18/fill-from-bg, is itself held),
;; so this stays a bare declaration, not a landing; retire this note once the
;; vitof12.xyzw gap above is fixed and the real defun replaces it.
(define-extern collide-list-fill-bg-using-box (function collide-cache collide-list collide-query none))


;; og:preserve-this function collide-list-fill-bg-using-line-sphere is deferred,
;; not landed. Its own decompiler fallback body is not valid GOAL (local-vars typed
;; none/pointer/matrix generically throughout past op 240, the same non-compiling
;; shape as output-race-mesh's deferred body). The blocker: s0 is read off a value
;; typed collide-hash-scratch at raw offset 172, a field that type does not declare
;; (its own layout is a 0-2047 collidable-bits/poly-bits/id-bits union plus a tris
;; field at 2048; 172 is not named anywhere in it), then dereferenced directly as a
;; pointer. A type_casts.jsonc entry forcing s0 to (pointer uint32) at the failing
;; op was tried and reverted; it did not change the error, so the real blocker is
;; upstream of that op (the offset-172 field itself resolving to the wrong source
;; type), not the final dereference. Nothing else in this file calls this function.
;; Retire this note once the real container type for the offset-172 read is
;; evidenced.
